      blurb: 'Steel scales and the snarling beast mask together: the full kit of a warlord’s chosen few, heavy as duty and as hard to take off. Not an inch of the man shows — a walking statue of his master’s importance.\nYet what does a statue guard when the master is gone? In 1644 rebels marched into Beijing. The last Ming emperor hanged himself behind his palace, and the masked guards found there was no one left to guard.\n“The last wall of a dynasty, or an empty mask. It all depended on who opened the gates of Beijing.”',
      patch: { extraMass: 0.265, protection: { blunt: 0.6, cut: 0.96, pierce: 0.7, regions: { head: { blunt: 0.68, cut: 0.97, pierce: 0.8 } } } },
